(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"8a049918-8ab1-544d-98d4-4f3e3be23d7f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"hg1", ",", " ", "hg2"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5b596779-8976-dc48-99b7-66e130ff339c"],
 " ",
 "gives True if hg1 and hg2 are isomorphic as labelled hypergraphs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"6e618bc0-fcfa-8943-adef-ded1c245e874"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"ef4486db-c875-f245-b6de-4bf104be35ed"],

Cell["\<\
Some renaming of vertex identifiers must carry hg1 onto hg2: the edge \
multisets must match exactly, each edge matching up to its own symmetry type, \
with edge multiplicities preserved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0b315d1f-c1d8-ac4c-ad61-eb0ca15e4a17"],

Cell["\<\
The renaming must also carry the labels of hg1 onto those of hg2 by a \
one-to-one correspondence. Labels are therefore significant only up to \
renaming: what must agree is which elements share a label, not what the \
labels are called.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"dd3a1c72-cf0b-0344-8823-409566e8c2a7"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels and edge labels are put in correspondence independently of one \
another.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e19a9eb4-8ddb-af42-be52-27d73c6c1f9c"],

Cell["\<\
An element with no label can correspond only to an element with no label. \
Without this, every unlabelled hypergraph would be isomorphic to a labelled \
one whose labels were all alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a5fbd200-0071-cd4f-ae36-11fc1a68026d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1d83b7bd-c05e-fb42-bb01-e5116b4361af"],
 " the skeletons are compared instead, ignoring labels altogether. Labelled \
isomorphism always implies isomorphism of skeletons."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5336a3e8-81a9-004e-8f2d-34e46193c333"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Method", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fbea7d2e-46ff-fc4e-9c42-d5776924c881"],
 " option is as for CanonicalHypergraph. Both settings always agree here."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0908aa8c-e610-4245-8994-5dd80704c83b"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive, and is comfortable up to roughly eight vertices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c1e10032-62ce-0142-bc37-7ad2473acd66"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"f79e2b8b-721a-1c44-91aa-c87271d80d42"],

Cell["The same directed path on different identifiers:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"8180d512-f3a9-7846-9e7a-ecbe284ac8af"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, \
{20, 30}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {1, \
3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"07b82637-8f34-f84e-b322-3babb21a10a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"506f9fcb-\
3777-4544-b74f-4b8a3a98ef00"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types are respected: a directed path is not an unordered one, but an \
unordered path on three vertices is an unordered star:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"84d3d7cd-db8e-bf49-adcc-8dad26891922"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{1, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0d473114-46aa-8441-b4ea-41bb55635740"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"4f959da7-\
aa8d-274d-b717-0db1cdf72df0"],

Cell["\<\
Labels count only up to a one-to-one renaming. Here a, b corresponds to x, y:\
\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"fa90ce87-c907-0c41-985d-7b4503bed22f"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c730d32f-de89-734c-bb60-346823e285ce"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"f19b2dd4-98f4-9640-9acb-6f2e00a3d8d7"],

Cell["\<\
But h3 repeats a single label where h1 has two distinct ones, and no \
correspondence can do that:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"3c2e7b2f-324c-ff40-863d-fb775546225c"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3], IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3, \"Labeled\" -> \
False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0d4f7113-b2bf-b54c-afda-91d1daca832a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"541992c1-\
fee3-8849-942c-3f71c385f64e"],

Cell["\<\
The same principle governs vertex labels. A, A, B against A, B, B is not an \
isomorphism, because A would have to correspond to both A and B:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"f770452d-0c0d-ff43-ae6d-2257c33a4612"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"C\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"C\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"A\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ea2cf68e-fe30-3540-9cfd-1646eec3c6bb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"32958596-\
9998-d44a-9fb2-74ee1c7a3217"],

Cell["An unlabelled edge is not a labelled one:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"d57bed33-d881-e04e-a93c-ec9516afa063"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}],
                       \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"96c66b46-8865-d142-ad6b-ee6f4d58e74e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"c6ca6948-\
726b-3c45-8a7d-1782c50ee2ca"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"edaf1cb3-31e3-d048-8fdd-6a45e5f9e5f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypergraph.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Canonical form and isomorphism",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c1ed094d-6dd1-d744-be1e-4ad4a6b550c9"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"ad859b3d-60aa-094d-9539-dd4dd8b99367"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindHypergraphIsomorphism", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b8de2109-1269-5540-9224-7890daa56cd4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"90bbd79f-c124-8448-a2ec-e064d266b3bf"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphSkeleton", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c1d76d53-73e6-ca42-85c6-31322df656d0"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "be544a25-02fd-9548-a39d-a335fb1752bd"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"bc1f2fb2-5847-7e44-aca6-1f77267b6f55"]
},
WindowSize->{800, 750},
